# Keep the repository LF-only in the working copy, not just in the index.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites a checkout to
# CRLF. That checkout still tests green on Windows, but fails the moment it is
# built somewhere else from the same files - a bind-mounted container, WSL, or
# an archive of the working tree - because the golden comparison only undoes
# CRLF when the test process itself runs on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden files are raw terminal output: escape sequences, control codes and
# carriage returns that carry meaning. They must round-trip byte for byte, so
# exempt them from conversion entirely rather than relying on eol=lf.
*.golden -text
